# lint-determinism.allow — the DST P0 determinism-fencing ratchet ledger.
# Companion: crates/_support/seams_init/tests/lint-determinism.sh. Precedent: lint-seam-installs.allow.
# Authority: docs/design/dst-and-wasm.md (branch docs/dst-wasm-scoping @
# 0d76f50dd), P0 phasing row + s3.3 blocking census.
#
# SEED: 2026-07-17 census regeneration @ origin/main 3fee87ff096c —
# cfg(test)-stripped, prod-only, a strictly tighter ledger than the doc's
# planning numbers (667 fs / 199 time). Seeded totals: fs 276 sites/64 files,
# time 230/46, rand 4/1, spawn 11/7, env 283/87, blocking 46/12.
# (Known census deltas, all explained: aio_uring's 6 fs + 4 time census sites
# sit inside #[cfg(all(test, target_os = "linux"))] and are correctly
# excluded here; spawn +1 = the dshash bench-rig, ledgered not hidden; rand
# ledgers only the raw-entropy internals of pg_strong_random — callers of
# pg_strong_random ARE the sanctioned route (s2.3) and are never flagged.)
#
# RESEED 2026-07-17b (review-fix charter, dst/p0-fencing-lint acceptance):
# pattern coverage expanded per the review's evasion census — the libc
# fs/time/env syscall surface (incl. libc::syscall), thread::sleep +
# libc sleep family (-> blocking), `use std::fs::{...}`/`use std::env::var`
# import-line idioms, std::env::set_var/remove_var — and the scanner made
# string/char-literal aware (a "//" or "/*" inside a literal no longer
# truncates or poisons the scan). Reseeded totals: fs 453 sites/90 files,
# time 243/56, rand 4/1, spawn 11/7, env 286/89, blocking 87/43. All 43
# row annotations from the seed ledger were ported verbatim. The growth is
# pattern coverage, not new code: same tree as the seed (origin/main
# 3fee87ff096c + this lint branch, which adds no production code).
#
# P1 RETIREMENT 2026-07-17c (dst/substrate compose — P1-VFS + P2 merged):
# the P1 fence conversions retired per the WS-C transplant spec
# (notes/dst-p1-ws-c-allowlist-rows.md, Batches 1-3): 19 fs rows deleted
# (fd copydir/io/reinit/temp/vfd; transam_xlog backup/removal/startup/write;
# slru, timeline, twophase, xlogarchive, xlogrecovery, basebackup,
# walsummarizer, controldata_utils, pgrcolumnar part_cache/segfile), 6 fs
# budgets shrunk (loadsort 11->7, reader 9->6, copy parallel.rs 4->1,
# fd desc.rs 8->4 + fd sync.rs 23->2 both keeping their # pending carve-out
# tags, alter_system 5->2), 1 time row deleted (walsummarizer mtime — the
# duration_since site now rides Vfs FileInfo). Three NEW fs rows, all
# DST-REVIEW(dst-compose)-marked: the vfs crate itself (posix.rs 35 = THE
# sanctioned syscall hub the fd/vfd choke fronts; lib.rs 4 = contract-surface
# tokens; sim.rs 1 = cfg(pgrust_sim)-only method name). Composed totals:
# fs 334 sites/74 files, time 182/34, rand 4/1, spawn 11/7, env 289/91,
# blocking 84/42 — allowlist == census exactly, 0 violations 0 warnings.
#
# WIDENING 2026-07-17d (P3-CENSUS, branch dst/p3-census @ dst/substrate
# e1a7e7b47 — the dst-p3-scheduler.md s7 Wave-1 ENTRY gate; charter: the
# s1.3 layer-2 widened re-census the adversarial review commissioned).
# FOUR NEW SECTIONS seeded below, existing rows untouched:
#   join 12/9, barrier 7/2, once 289/91, scope 6/4 — allowlist == widened
#   census exactly, 0 violations 0 warnings at seed.
# Every widened-arm site maps to a s3 conversion row (14/15/18/19), a
# sanctioned type (pg_barrier in nodehash), or a ledgered name collision
# (the lifecycle armed join in runtime/sched.rs) — NO new unclassified
# blocking class was found. Two sites are NEW versus the design's own row
# lists (writer.rs finalize-path join L996; the explicit scoped pump join
# copy/parallel.rs L1506) — flagged in notes/dst-p3-census.md. Lock waits
# are deliberately NOT a section here (not statically lintable — see the
# lint header; s1.3 layer 1 owns that class at runtime).
#
# ROW FORMAT (tab-separated):
#   <category>\t<file>\t<max-sites>[\t<annotation>]
# <max-sites> is the file's site budget: matching production source lines
# the lint tolerates. Categories: fs time rand spawn env blocking
# join barrier once scope.
#
# THE RATCHET LAW:
#   * budgets may only SHRINK; rows may only be DELETED;
#   * a NEW row (or a raised budget) must carry a review marker in the
#     annotation column — "DST-REVIEW(<who>): <why>". This is a REVIEW
#     CONVENTION enforced by humans diffing this file (the lint cannot
#     tell a new row from a seeded one); the lint's contribution is
#     CONFIG-FAILing malformed markers/duplicate rows/budget<1, and
#     surfacing every marker row as a NOTE on every run so train diffs
#     carry the exception visibly. Never add an unmarked row: the fix for
#     a new raw site is routing it through its category's sanctioned
#     surface (fs: fd/vfd Vfs choke s2.1; time: WaiterClock/
#     timestamp_seams s2.2; rand: pg_strong_random s2.3; spawn:
#     launch_backend spawner seam s3.3; env: knobs registry s2.5;
#     blocking: Waiter/eventcount per the runtime/src/rg.rs precedent
#     s3.3).
#   * rows whose sites vanished (WARN(stale-allowlist)) are deleted, and
#     shrink warnings (WARN(shrink-budget)) are honored by lowering budgets.
#
# ACCEPTED LIMITS of the grep-family scanner (what a row here does and does
# not promise) are ledgered in the header of crates/_support/seams_init/tests/lint-determinism.sh —
# read them before arguing a count with the lint.
#
# The fs section is grouped per crate with per-crate subtotals so the P1-VFS
# lanes can retire whole sections as each wave lands (s2.1 wiring order:
# fd/vfd -> transam_xlog remnants -> pgrcolumnar CbIo fence -> long tail).
#
# REGENERATION (audit/reseed under explicit charter ONLY — regen resurrects
# deleted rows and drops annotations, which the ratchet law forbids as a
# routine operation):
#     crates/_support/seams_init/tests/lint-determinism.sh --regen > crates/_support/seams_init/tests/lint-determinism.allow
#
# SE delta: scripts/lint-determinism.se-delta.md (reference only; applied by
# the single-executor reconciler when SE lands, NOT enforced on main).


